  "closed": true,
  "commits": [
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "49377ac19afbddb181efcd814e780b5e09490a73",
      "subject": "Fix preferred execution dispatch so partial/custom self-hosted selectors such as `192t` match persisted optimizer observations that record the runner's full label set, allowing preferred shapes like AMSRE's 48p/8t to survive dispatch instead of falling back to the default 4p planner. Change automatic single-detector sharding to one shard per active pipeline, capped by parameter-space size, while retaining the existing positive-integer shards-per-pipeline manual override. Binary-refine remains single-shard because its search is sequential, and aggregate multi-detector runs retain one detector task per worker queue entry. Updated workflow text and regression coverage; all 658 tests pass."
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "b147689e46b1a0f06e78e8f89d7c97d53cf9722d",
      "subject": "Fix execution-optimizer early stopping so a perceived throughput peak is only accepted after throughput falls strictly more than 2% below the best observed rate on both available sides of the entire \u22642% peak/plateau region. Plateaus remain part of the peak until an outer measurement crosses that threshold; peaks touching a legal pipeline boundary use the necessary one-sided rule, and completely flat ranges finish normally instead of inventing a peak. The workflow now passes legal pipeline bounds into the assessment, reports the new bracketing rule, and removes the obsolete three-consecutive-shape logic. Added regression coverage for interior peaks, exact-2% boundaries, plateaus, one-sided boundary peaks, and flat ranges; all 655 tests pass."
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "bdc0ea3be422f9cccdeca35f25cb8b1760102295",
      "subject": "Fix optimizer benchmark evidence consumption by preferred regression shape resolution. The optimizer was persisting the new Doc-UFCN 5p/76t measurements correctly, but the shared workload matcher rejected benchmark-limited optimizer observations because it required actual_parameter_sets to equal the detector's full possible_parameter_sets. It now treats a completed optimizer benchmark as complete when actual_parameter_sets equals min(possible_parameter_sets, optimizer_benchmark_parameter_sets), matching the persistence layer's existing comparability rule. The detector-implementation compatibility fallback uses that same canonical matcher, preventing a second definition of valid optimizer evidence. Added regression coverage proving a 2000-set detector optimized with a 256-set benchmark resolves the stored 5p/76t preferred shape instead of falling back to auto sharding. All 651 unittest tests pass."
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "21ab8a2b61be4a4f5636ca5027b63e6b1d4a5fdf",
      "subject": "Harden report Python bootstrap on self-hosted runners"
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "4b319fe7310400014e6bba335c8d7cf19d82f897",
      "subject": "Canonicalize execution-shape scaling without changing exhaustive semantics"
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "351cca1badb08067ad7c8029d9b3a7b2bb58999c",
      "subject": "Fix the optimizer Actions plot/table mismatch at its actual source: the job summary was embedding the results repository's `main`-branch SVG before the new optimizer intelligence had been published. GitHub could therefore fetch and cache the previous run's plot under the current run's unique query string, leaving the current-run shape table paired with a stale runner/profile plot. The optimizer now publishes first, resolves the resulting results-repository commit, and only then writes the Actions summary with the heatmap pinned to that exact immutable commit. This preserves the existing run-local plot generation while guaranteeing the summary's plot and shape table come from the same optimizer execution. Added workflow coverage for publish-before-summary ordering and commit-pinned SVG URLs; all 647 unittest tests pass."
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "9f63435616f32987d8d78499adcb48713d6fdf9f",
      "subject": "Harden reusable results-repository checkout hygiene"
    },
    {
      "author": "Dan Stupka",
      "sha": "71a8b432f7121f2bc4c9fe37c0e58028f65f2ad5",
      "subject": "Canonicalize contracted parameter-domain counts"
    },
    {
